IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aa-intestacy`

-- Administration Act 1903 (WA), ss 12A, 13(1a), 14, 15, 25, 33, 36, 55, 139 and 71 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_administration-act-1903.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (subjects/au/scenarios/wa-cradle-to-grave-*): Sue dies intestate on 27 January 2060, widowed since
-- Graham's death on 19 August 2052, leaving Chloe (56) and Jake (53) (chloe c088, jake k088: "half each"). Jake dies intestate
-- on 2 May 2079, divorced since 2039, leaving Ruby (46); "an estate of $38,000 and the apartment" (jake k098). Graham's will
-- leaves everything to Sue with Chloe as executor (chloe c087, jake k084: Jake takes "no"). The scenarios give no value for
-- Sue's estate or Jake's apartment, so the dollar figures used with them below are the encoder's, chosen for arithmetic.

